{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>His aunt.</b> She is his uncle's wife." "<b>They shall die childless.</b> The Sadducees say it is like ערומים [naked], and the meaning of ימותו is like יומתו [shall be put to death], and they did not speak truth. The correct interpretation is as the Aramaic translator said, and I have already explained כתבו את האיש הזה ערירי, for it is like הולך ערירי [one who walks childless]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The phrase כתבו את האיש הזה ערירי appears to cite 1 Chronicles 2:30, though the exact form with כתבו is textually unusual; rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:25.768249083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}